data floor_component_receipt_note: String = "The floor's per-COMPONENT receipt, machine-readable, written on every exit path including a red one. WHY IT EXISTS, priced: .github/workflows/falsifier-alert.yml read only the overall workflow conclusion and hardcoded one causal story for every failure — 'affected-set cold control is dark, per-PR selection UNVERIFIED, Gate-1 receipts do not execute'. On run 30509024051 all three clauses were FALSE: the predict-only affected-set control concluded Done over 5217 witnesses and the expect_red batches produced their receipts; the single failing component was the silent-pick gate, killed at its whole-receipt wall budget. An overall-red composite that erases the green state of its completed children is a state-space conflation (DESIGN section 5), and it misdirects triage every time it fires. This module is the projection that makes the alert read state instead of inferring it. THE RECORD IS NOT NEW: each component is one batch-grain Concluded std.observation.ObservationEvent — the same authority gunbc.witness_row_cost names as THE record ('not a TSV schema') — so Refused stays distinct from Failed and a budget kill is TimedOut with its budget and elapsed, not a flattened red. A bespoke status schema here would have been a second representation of that record (DESIGN section 3)."

data floor_component_receipt_role_note: String = "Components are identified by STRUCTURAL ROLE, never by batch index. Indices are not stable: gunbc_falsifier_batches composes conditionally on enrollment flags (falsifier_self_host_wet_batch_enrolled and siblings), so one flag flip shifts every later index — which is why the silent-pick gate reports as batch 4 today while sitting fifth in source order. An alert keyed on 'batch 1' would relocate the hardcoded assumption rather than remove it. The affected-set cold control is instead identified by the property that DEFINES it: node_frontier_selection = SelectionPredictOnly, reusing the std.realization_schedule authority (the per-PR corpus counterpart is SelectionApplied). Ambiguity fails closed: zero predict-only components yields ControlAbsent and two or more yields ControlAmbiguous, never a guess."

data floor_component_receipt_timed_out_frontier_note: String = "TimedOut is MODELLED and PROJECTED here but the floor does not yet emit it, and that gap is declared rather than papered over. A whole-receipt wall-budget kill carries its numbers structurally at the point it is raised — v1_interpreter InterpError::WitnessWallBudgetExceeded { elapsed_ms, budget_ms } — but ClaimOutcome::RuntimeError flattens them to a formatted String before the walk sees them, so the executor cannot fill TimedOut's budget and elapsed without re-parsing its own prose. It therefore emits Refused with the interpreter's own located diagnostic, which is not a downgrade: a kill at a declared ceiling IS the deliberate, located stop that observation_refused_distinct_note defines Refused to mean. Fabricating 0 for budget and elapsed to reach the more specific arm would be the fabricated-plausible-output DESIGN section 5 forbids. Dissolve-on: ClaimOutcome carries the typed WitnessWallBudgetExceeded pair through to ClaimResult, at which point the budget arm becomes TimedOut and this note deletes. The projection side needs no change then — floor_component_outcome_of_tag already admits the tag and floor_component_outcome_members already renders the fields, proven by execution today. The arm now also names its CLOCK (std.measure ClockBasis, operator ruling 2026-08-05), and the wall-budget kill this note is about is exactly why: a whole-receipt wall ceiling and the fast-lane thread-CPU fail-stop both surface as TimedOut, so the clock is what tells them apart. floor_component_outcome_of_tag takes the basis as a parameter rather than assuming one, because the tag alone has never carried it."

data floor_component_receipt_seed_transport_deferral_note: String = "PURE BOOTSTRAP RECEIPT for the seed-side transport this module is consumed by (review 45058 asked for it, correctly — new hand-Rust owes a named deferral, not a description). WHAT IS ADDED: no new Rust file and no parallel authority — functions inside the existing claim_executor bin that locate this module, resolve it, call floor_component_row_of_failure_mode / floor_component_receipt_document, and write the returned bytes. WHAT IS NOT IN RUST: the receipt's shape, its schema, the failure-mode-to-outcome mapping, the role identification, and every judgment about success — all of that is here, under dag/test/claim/floor_component_receipt_witness_test.dag. The seed side carries no classification of its own; its `_ => failed` catch-all was removed in favour of floor_component_outcome_of_failure_mode's refusal arm. BOUNDARY SHAPE: the seed calls millisecond(count:) through the interpreter and hands back the resulting Millisecond, so no carrier is constructed in Rust and no flat-scalar duration crosses the seam. The sibling seam gunbc.observation_seed_render (render_phase_concluded_line, same bin) still takes elapsed_ms: Nat; that is un-migrated debt on its own lane and was deliberately NOT copied here. DEFERRED TO: the v1 exit finish line ZeroHandMaintainedRust, roadmap node v1-zero-hand-maintained-rust (gunbc.v1_deletion_plan v1_exit_finish_lines). CONCRETE DISSOLUTION: the transport deletes when the floor's receipt write is issued from .dag as a typed host effect (Filesystem.Write through host_effect_apply, the shell-to-intent Phase 2 routing for runtime-present sites) instead of std::fs::write in the seed — at that point the resolve-and-call marshalling has no reason to exist and this module's document function is invoked directly by the emitted walk."

data floor_component_receipt_unit_surface_note: String = "Every duration on this module's public surface is the std.measure carrier Millisecond (= Measure<Time, Milli, Nat>, the ratified Measure<Q,S,M> shape), never a bare Nat named *_ms. Two independent reviews (review 45058, review 45070) flagged the earlier *_ms: Nat constructor parameters, and they were right: a duration whose unit lives only in the field name is form 3 of the standing unit-modeling merge-hold, and the fact that a sibling seed seam still spells it that way makes that seam debt rather than a licence. Immediate millisecond(count:) wrapping inside the body does NOT discharge it — the parameter surface is what callers can get wrong, and a caller passing seconds into wall_ms would have typechecked. The seed constructs no carrier: it calls millisecond(count:) across the interpreter boundary and passes the Millisecond back in, so the constructor stays the single authority (a Value::Record built in Rust would have forked it). There is exactly ONE seed entry point, floor_component_row_of_failure_mode, whose failure_mode vocabulary covers every disposition the walk can report including not_reached."

data floor_component_receipt_schema: String = "floor-component-receipt/v1"

data floor_component_resource_checkpoint_note: String = "OPERATOR RULING 2026-08-13 (#8239 → #8163): this receipt is a per-component RESOURCE CHECKPOINT for alert routing — batch/component outcomes, run_terminal incomplete envelope, selection degradation — NOT a second observation ledger and NOT a carrier for the exact active workset. Subject identity (entry/module/phase) and live measurements (RSS, swap, PSI, progress) belong on the one attempt ledger #8163 lands (std.observation RecordedObservation at target/floor-attempts/<attempt>/events/<producer>.jsonl, carrier a974f44 / sunny-pike-825), which the coordinator tails. A receipt field named active_workset would be empty by construction at every checkpoint the sequential floor writes today, while the subjects it would have named ride GUNBC_FLOOR_PHASE_JOURNAL instead — two channels reconciled by hand is the split the ruling refuses. The field is therefore absent from this schema; fold absorption into #8163 rather than mint a parallel authority here."

data floor_component_phase_journal_scaffold_note: String = "TEMPORARY PROJECTION (operator ruling 2026-08-13, verdict bound to #8239 head): GUNBC_FLOOR_PHASE_JOURNAL active-workset admit/completed rows are the interim channel for in-flight witness identity until measurements and subjects emit as RecordedObservation events on the #8163 per-producer ledger (own producer identity — sequence-checked files refuse a second writer). Dissolve-on: #8163 carrier on main + floor walk emits subject/measurement events through that ledger; delete journal rows and cli_run active-workset append once FLOOR2 reducer consumes the ledger path green by execution."

data floor_component_receipt_path: String = "target/floor-component-receipt.json"

data floor_component_receipt_artifact_name: String = "floor-component-receipt"

data floor_component_failure_mode_edge_note: String = "WHY THE MODE RIDES BESIDE THE OUTCOME INSTEAD OF BEING RECOVERED FROM IT. floor_component_outcome_of_failure_mode is deliberately many-to-one: Infra and WitnessRed BOTH map to Failed, because both are a component that broke and ObservationOutcome is the right grain for the observation record. But they are not the same fault and they do not route to the same place — Infra is the fleet's (a runner died, a toolchain went missing), WitnessRed is the witness owner's (a claim is genuinely false). A consumer holding only the Failed arm cannot tell them apart, so it either routes both to one owner or re-derives the class by sniffing the diagnostic prose, which is the string-classification this module already refuses at the seed boundary. The mode therefore rides ON THE ROW, at row grain, and std.observation is NOT widened: ObservationOutcome stays the canonical record of WHAT the transition was, and the mode records WHICH declared failure vocabulary produced it. The two are derived from ONE tag in one place (floor_component_row_of_failure_mode), so they cannot disagree — a row whose mode says Infra while its outcome says Done is not constructible through the seed path. ModeUnrecorded is the honest arm for the tag-built constructor, which is handed an outcome directly and genuinely never saw a mode; the seed path never produces it."

type FloorComponentRow {
  event: ObservationEvent
  selection: NodeFrontierSelection
  witnesses: Nat
  failure_mode: FloorComponentFailureMode
}

type FloorControlState
  = ControlConcluded { row: FloorComponentRow }
  | ControlAbsent { cause: NonEmptyStr }
  | ControlAmbiguous { cause: NonEmptyStr, matched: Nat }

fn floor_component_subject(run_id: NonEmptyStr, index: Nat, label: NonEmptyStr) -> ObservationSubject {
  ObservationSubject {
    segments: [
      RunSegment { id: run_id },
      BatchSegment { index: index, label: label }
    ]
  }
}

fn floor_component_selection_of_tag(tag: NonEmptyStr) -> NodeFrontierSelection? {
  if (tag as String) == "predict_only" { Present { value: SelectionPredictOnly } }
  else if (tag as String) == "applied" { Present { value: SelectionApplied } }
  else if (tag as String) == "off" { Present { value: SelectionOff } }
  else if (tag as String) == "sampled" { Present { value: SelectionSampled } }
  else { none }
}

fn floor_component_selection_tag(s: NodeFrontierSelection) -> String {
  match s {
    SelectionOff => "off"
    SelectionApplied => "applied"
    SelectionPredictOnly => "predict_only"
    SelectionSampled => "sampled"
  }
}

fn floor_component_outcome_of_tag(
  tag: NonEmptyStr,
  detail: NonEmptyStr,
  basis: ClockBasis,
  budget: Millisecond,
  elapsed: Millisecond,
  shown_failures: Nat
) -> ObservationOutcome? {
  if (tag as String) == "done" { Present { value: Done } }
  else if (tag as String) == "refused" { Present { value: Refused { diagnostic: detail } } }
  else if (tag as String) == "failed" { Present { value: Failed { error: detail, output: "" } } }
  else if (tag as String) == "timed_out" {
    Present { value: TimedOut { basis: basis, budget: budget, elapsed: elapsed } }
  }
  else if (tag as String) == "skipped" { Present { value: Skipped { reason: detail } } }
  else if (tag as String) == "final" { Present { value: Final { shown_failures: shown_failures } } }
  else { none }
}

data floor_component_failure_mode_note: String = "The seed's failure-mode vocabulary (claim_executor falsifier_failure_mode: BudgetExceeded | Infra | WitnessRed, plus the no-failures case) mapped onto ObservationOutcome HERE rather than in Rust, so the classification sits under a witness and the seed transport carries no judgment of its own. BudgetExceeded becomes Refused, not Failed: a kill at a declared ceiling is the deliberate, located stop observation_refused_distinct_note defines Refused to mean, and its remedy (re-basis the dated ceiling, or fix the row's cost) differs from a broken witness's. UNKNOWN MODE REFUSES. The first version of this mapping lived in the seed with a `_ => failed` catch-all, which would have absorbed a newly added mode into `failed` silently — a widen with no diagnostic, exactly the absorbing fallback DESIGN section 5 forbids. Here an unmodelled mode returns absent, the row cannot be built, and the walk fails closed with the mode named."

fn floor_component_outcome_of_failure_mode(mode: NonEmptyStr, detail: NonEmptyStr) -> ObservationOutcome? {
  match floor_component_failure_mode_of(mode: mode) {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: m } => floor_component_outcome_of_mode(m: m, detail: detail)
  }
}

fn floor_component_outcome_members(o: ObservationOutcome) -> List<JsonKeyValue> {
  match o {
    Done => []
    Refused { diagnostic: d } => [json_kv(key: "diagnostic", value: json_string(s: d as String))]
    Failed { error: e, output: out } => [
      json_kv(key: "error", value: json_string(s: e as String)),
      json_kv(key: "output", value: json_string(s: out))
    ]
    TimedOut { basis: _, budget: b, elapsed: el } => [
      json_kv(key: "budget_ms", value: json_int(n: millisecond_count(m: b))),
      json_kv(key: "elapsed_ms", value: json_int(n: millisecond_count(m: el)))
    ]
    Skipped { reason: r } => [json_kv(key: "reason", value: json_string(s: r as String))]
    Final { shown_failures: n } => [json_kv(key: "shown_failures", value: json_int(n: n))]
  }
}

fn floor_component_transition_outcome(t: ObservationTransition) -> ObservationOutcome? {
  match t {
    Begin => none
    Step { k: _, n: _ } => none
    Concluded { outcome: o } => Present { value: o }
  }
}

fn floor_component_row_of(
  run_id: NonEmptyStr,
  index: Nat,
  label: NonEmptyStr,
  selection: NodeFrontierSelection,
  witnesses: Nat,
  outcome: ObservationOutcome,
  wall: Millisecond,
  failure_mode: FloorComponentFailureMode
) -> FloorComponentRow {
  FloorComponentRow {
    event: ObservationEvent {
      subject: floor_component_subject(run_id: run_id, index: index, label: label),
      transition: Concluded { outcome: outcome },
      durations: observation_durations_wall(elapsed: millisecond_to_nanosecond(m: wall)),
      rss: MeasuredUnavailable { cause: "per-component RSS not sampled by the floor walk" as NonEmptyStr }
    },
    selection: selection,
    witnesses: witnesses,
    failure_mode: failure_mode
  }
}

fn floor_component_row(
  run_id: NonEmptyStr,
  index: Nat,
  label: NonEmptyStr,
  selection_tag: NonEmptyStr,
  witnesses: Nat,
  outcome_tag: NonEmptyStr,
  detail: NonEmptyStr,
  basis: ClockBasis,
  budget: Millisecond,
  elapsed: Millisecond,
  shown_failures: Nat,
  wall: Millisecond
) -> FloorComponentRow? {
  match floor_component_selection_of_tag(tag: selection_tag) {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: sel } =>
      match floor_component_outcome_of_tag(
        tag: outcome_tag,
        detail: detail,
        basis: basis,
        budget: budget,
        elapsed: elapsed,
        shown_failures: shown_failures
      ) {
        Absent => none
        Present { value: outcome } => Present {
          value: floor_component_row_of(
            run_id: run_id,
            index: index,
            label: label,
            selection: sel,
            witnesses: witnesses,
            outcome: outcome,
            wall: wall,
            failure_mode: ModeUnrecorded
          )
        }
      }
  }
}

fn floor_component_row_of_failure_mode(
  run_id: NonEmptyStr,
  index: Nat,
  label: NonEmptyStr,
  selection_tag: NonEmptyStr,
  witnesses: Nat,
  failure_mode: NonEmptyStr,
  detail: NonEmptyStr,
  wall: Millisecond
) -> FloorComponentRow? {
  match floor_component_selection_of_tag(tag: selection_tag) {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: sel } =>
      match floor_component_failure_mode_of(mode: failure_mode) {
        Absent => none
        Present { value: mode } =>
          match floor_component_outcome_of_mode(m: mode, detail: detail) {
            Absent => none
            Present { value: outcome } => Present {
              value: floor_component_row_of(
                run_id: run_id,
                index: index,
                label: label,
                selection: sel,
                witnesses: witnesses,
                outcome: outcome,
                wall: wall,
                failure_mode: mode
              )
            }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn floor_component_row_not_concluded(
  run_id: NonEmptyStr,
  index: Nat,
  label: NonEmptyStr,
  selection_tag: NonEmptyStr,
  failure_mode: NonEmptyStr,
  detail: NonEmptyStr
) -> FloorComponentRow? {
  match floor_component_selection_of_tag(tag: selection_tag) {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: sel } =>
      match floor_component_failure_mode_of(mode: failure_mode) {
        Absent => none
        Present { value: mode } => Present {
          value: FloorComponentRow {
            event: ObservationEvent {
              subject: floor_component_subject(run_id: run_id, index: index, label: label),
              transition: Begin,
              durations: observation_durations_wall(
                elapsed: millisecond_to_nanosecond(m: millisecond(count: 0))
              ),
              rss: MeasuredUnavailable {
                cause: "per-component RSS not sampled by the floor walk" as NonEmptyStr
              }
            },
            selection: sel,
            witnesses: 0,
            failure_mode: mode
          }
        }
      }
  }
}

fn floor_component_row_index(row: FloorComponentRow) -> Nat {
  fold(row.event.subject.segments, init: 0, f: (acc, seg) =>
    match seg {
      RunSegment { id: _ } => acc
      BatchSegment { index: i, label: _ } => i
      EntrySegment { source_path: _ } => acc
      ModuleSegment { module_path: _ } => acc
      DeclarationSegment { declaration: _ } => acc
      PhaseSegment { name: _ } => acc
    })
}

fn floor_component_row_label(row: FloorComponentRow) -> String {
  fold(row.event.subject.segments, init: "", f: (acc, seg) =>
    match seg {
      RunSegment { id: _ } => acc
      BatchSegment { index: _, label: l } => l as String
      EntrySegment { source_path: _ } => acc
      ModuleSegment { module_path: _ } => acc
      DeclarationSegment { declaration: _ } => acc
      PhaseSegment { name: _ } => acc
    })
}

fn floor_component_wall_members(w: Measured<Nanosecond>) -> List<JsonKeyValue> {
  match w {
    MeasuredValue { value: ns } => [
      json_kv(key: "wall_ms", value: json_int(n: nanosecond_count(n: ns) / 1000000))
    ]
    MeasuredUnavailable { cause: c } => [
      json_kv(key: "wall_ms", value: json_null()),
      json_kv(key: "wall_unavailable_cause", value: json_string(s: c as String))
    ]
  }
}

data floor_component_is_done_locality_note: String = "Why this predicate is LOCAL and not a std.observation addition (review 45058 asked for the canonical fold/query surface instead). Checked: std.observation exposes observation_outcome_class and observation_outcome_is_anomaly, and BOTH are themselves total hand-written matches over ObservationOutcome — there is no fold or query surface over that coproduct to consume, so sibling-style matching IS the canonical shape at the authority. It is also not a fork of is_anomaly, which answers a different question and disagrees on two arms: Skipped is NOT an anomaly (nothing broke) yet is plainly not Done, and Final is not an anomaly either. So !observation_outcome_is_anomaly would report a skipped batch as successful — the exact conflation this receipt exists to prevent. Routing through observation_outcome_class would replace 6 arms with 10 and still lose the Final { shown_failures } reading. Kept local under second-consumer discipline (DESIGN section 6, model just-in-time): it has exactly one consumer today. Dissolve-on: a SECOND consumer needs a component-success predicate, at which point it lifts to std.observation beside observation_outcome_is_anomaly and this row deletes."

fn floor_component_row_is_done(row: FloorComponentRow) -> Bool {
  match floor_component_transition_outcome(t: row.event.transition) {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: o } =>
      match o {
        Done => true
        Refused { diagnostic: _ } => false
        Failed { error: _, output: _ } => false
        TimedOut { basis: _, budget: _, elapsed: _ } => false
        Skipped { reason: _ } => false
        Final { shown_failures: n } => n == 0
      }
  }
}

fn floor_component_row_json(row: FloorComponentRow) -> JsonValue {
  match floor_component_transition_outcome(t: row.event.transition) {
    Absent => json_object(members: [
      json_kv(key: "index", value: json_int(n: floor_component_row_index(row: row))),
      json_kv(key: "label", value: json_string(s: floor_component_row_label(row: row))),
      json_kv(key: "selection", value: json_string(s: floor_component_selection_tag(s: row.selection))),
      json_kv(key: "outcome", value: json_string(s: floor_component_outcome_wire_tag(r: ComponentNotConcluded))),
      json_kv(key: "failure_mode", value: json_string(s: floor_component_failure_mode_tag(m: row.failure_mode)))
    ])
    Present { value: o } => json_object(members: concat(
      [
        json_kv(key: "index", value: json_int(n: floor_component_row_index(row: row))),
        json_kv(key: "label", value: json_string(s: floor_component_row_label(row: row))),
        json_kv(key: "selection", value: json_string(s: floor_component_selection_tag(s: row.selection))),
        json_kv(key: "witnesses", value: json_int(n: row.witnesses)),
        json_kv(key: "outcome", value: json_string(s: floor_component_outcome_wire_tag(r: ComponentConcluded { outcome: o }))),
        json_kv(key: "failure_mode", value: json_string(s: floor_component_failure_mode_tag(m: row.failure_mode))),
        json_kv(key: "is_affected_set_cold_control", value: json_bool(
          b: node_frontier_selection_eq(left: row.selection, right: SelectionPredictOnly)
        ))
      ],
      concat(
        floor_component_outcome_members(o: o),
        floor_component_wall_members(w: observation_wall(event: row.event))
      )
    ))
  }
}

fn floor_affected_set_control_rows(rows: List<FloorComponentRow>) -> List<FloorComponentRow> {
  rows |> filter(r => node_frontier_selection_eq(left: r.selection, right: SelectionPredictOnly))
}

fn floor_affected_set_control_state(rows: List<FloorComponentRow>) -> FloorControlState {
  let matched = floor_affected_set_control_rows(rows: rows)
  let n = count(matched)
  if n > 1 {
    ControlAmbiguous {
      cause: "more than one SelectionPredictOnly component — the cold control is not uniquely identified" as NonEmptyStr,
      matched: n
    }
  } else {
    match matched.first() {
      Absent => ControlAbsent {
        cause: "no SelectionPredictOnly component in this receipt — the affected-set cold control did not run" as NonEmptyStr
      }
      Present { value: r } => ControlConcluded { row: r }
    }
  }
}

fn floor_affected_set_control_json(rows: List<FloorComponentRow>) -> JsonValue {
  match floor_affected_set_control_state(rows: rows) {
    ControlConcluded { row: r } => json_object(members: [
      json_kv(key: "state", value: json_string(s: "present")),
      json_kv(key: "verified", value: json_bool(b: floor_component_row_is_done(row: r))),
      json_kv(key: "component", value: floor_component_row_json(row: r))
    ])
    ControlAbsent { cause: c } => json_object(members: [
      json_kv(key: "state", value: json_string(s: "absent")),
      json_kv(key: "verified", value: json_bool(b: false)),
      json_kv(key: "cause", value: json_string(s: c as String))
    ])
    ControlAmbiguous { cause: c, matched: m } => json_object(members: [
      json_kv(key: "state", value: json_string(s: "ambiguous")),
      json_kv(key: "verified", value: json_bool(b: false)),
      json_kv(key: "cause", value: json_string(s: c as String)),
      json_kv(key: "matched", value: json_int(n: m))
    ])
  }
}

fn floor_unsuccessful_component_rows(rows: List<FloorComponentRow>) -> List<FloorComponentRow> {
  rows |> filter(r => !floor_component_row_is_done(row: r))
}

fn floor_run_terminal_json(
  disposition: NonEmptyStr,
  cause: NonEmptyStr,
  concluded_count: Nat,
  pending_from_index: Nat
) -> JsonValue {
  json_object(members: [
    json_kv(key: "disposition", value: json_string(s: disposition as String)),
    json_kv(key: "cause", value: json_string(s: cause as String)),
    json_kv(key: "concluded_count", value: json_int(n: concluded_count)),
    json_kv(key: "pending_from_index", value: json_int(n: pending_from_index))
  ])
}

fn floor_component_receipt_json_value(
  workflow_name: NonEmptyStr,
  run_id: NonEmptyStr,
  head_sha: CommitSha,
  rows: List<FloorComponentRow>,
  selection_present: Bool,
  selection_mode_tag: NonEmptyStr,
  selected: Nat,
  total: Nat,
  categorization_unavailable: Bool,
  categorization_reason: String,
  run_terminal_present: Bool,
  run_terminal_disposition: NonEmptyStr,
  run_terminal_cause: NonEmptyStr,
  concluded_count: Nat,
  pending_from_index: Nat
) -> JsonValue {
  let base = [
    json_kv(key: receipt_member_schema, value: json_string(s: floor_component_receipt_schema)),
    json_kv(key: receipt_member_workflow_name, value: json_string(s: workflow_name as String)),
    json_kv(key: receipt_member_run_id, value: json_string(s: run_id as String)),
    json_kv(key: receipt_member_head_sha, value: json_string(s: head_sha as String)),
    json_kv(key: receipt_member_component_count, value: json_int(n: count(rows))),
    json_kv(key: receipt_member_affected_set_cold_control, value: floor_affected_set_control_json(rows: rows)),
    json_kv(key: receipt_member_unsuccessful_components, value: json_array(
      elements: floor_unsuccessful_component_rows(rows: rows) |> map(r => floor_component_row_json(row: r))
    )),
    json_kv(key: receipt_member_components, value: json_array(
      elements: rows |> map(r => floor_component_row_json(row: r))
    ))
  ]
  let with_terminal = if run_terminal_present {
    concat(base, [
      json_kv(
        key: receipt_member_run_terminal,
        value: floor_run_terminal_json(
          disposition: run_terminal_disposition,
          cause: run_terminal_cause,
          concluded_count: concluded_count,
          pending_from_index: pending_from_index
        )
      )
    ])
  } else {
    concat(base, [
      json_kv(key: receipt_member_run_terminal, value: json_null())
    ])
  }
  if selection_present {
    json_object(members: concat(with_terminal, [
      json_kv(
        key: receipt_member_selection_degradation,
        value: selection_degradation_receipt_json(
          selection_mode_tag: selection_mode_tag,
          selected: selected,
          total: total,
          categorization_unavailable: categorization_unavailable,
          categorization_reason: categorization_reason
        )
      )
    ]))
  } else {
    json_object(members: concat(with_terminal, [
      json_kv(key: receipt_member_selection_degradation, value: json_null())
    ]))
  }
}

data selection_degradation_always_emitted_note: String = "selection_degradation IS EMITTED ON EVERY PATH, INCLUDING THE ONE WITH NO SELECTION SNAPSHOT, where it is an explicit null. It previously appeared only when a snapshot existed, and the member was simply absent otherwise.\n\nThat was tolerable while nothing decoded the receipt. It stopped being tolerable the moment gunbc.floor_component_receipt_document made the member REQUIRED on the read side: the writer could still emit a document the reader would refuse, so encode-then-decode was broken for exactly the path claim_executor takes when no selection ran (review 49594 caught this, correctly, along with a note on the decoder side that overstated what this writer did).\n\nAn explicit null is the right repair rather than relaxing the decoder, because the two states differ and the receipt should say which one it is: `null` means this run had no selection degradation to report, and an ABSENT member means the writer did not tell you either way. Making absence impossible on the write side is what lets the read side treat absence as the defect it now is."

fn floor_component_receipt_document(
  workflow_name: NonEmptyStr,
  run_id: NonEmptyStr,
  head_sha: CommitSha,
  rows: List<FloorComponentRow>
) -> String {
  serialize_json(v: floor_component_receipt_json_value(
    workflow_name: workflow_name,
    run_id: run_id,
    head_sha: head_sha,
    rows: rows,
    selection_present: false,
    selection_mode_tag: "off" as NonEmptyStr,
    selected: 0,
    total: 0,
    categorization_unavailable: false,
    categorization_reason: "",
    run_terminal_present: false,
    run_terminal_disposition: "concluded" as NonEmptyStr,
    run_terminal_cause: "none" as NonEmptyStr,
    concluded_count: count(rows),
    pending_from_index: 0
  ))
}

fn floor_component_receipt_document_incomplete(
  workflow_name: NonEmptyStr,
  run_id: NonEmptyStr,
  head_sha: CommitSha,
  rows: List<FloorComponentRow>,
  run_terminal_cause: NonEmptyStr,
  concluded_count: Nat,
  pending_from_index: Nat
) -> String {
  serialize_json(v: floor_component_receipt_json_value(
    workflow_name: workflow_name,
    run_id: run_id,
    head_sha: head_sha,
    rows: rows,
    selection_present: false,
    selection_mode_tag: "off" as NonEmptyStr,
    selected: 0,
    total: 0,
    categorization_unavailable: false,
    categorization_reason: "",
    run_terminal_present: true,
    run_terminal_disposition: "incomplete" as NonEmptyStr,
    run_terminal_cause: run_terminal_cause,
    concluded_count: concluded_count,
    pending_from_index: pending_from_index
  ))
}

fn floor_component_receipt_document_incomplete_with_selection(
  workflow_name: NonEmptyStr,
  run_id: NonEmptyStr,
  head_sha: CommitSha,
  rows: List<FloorComponentRow>,
  run_terminal_cause: NonEmptyStr,
  concluded_count: Nat,
  pending_from_index: Nat,
  selection_mode_tag: NonEmptyStr,
  selected: Nat,
  total: Nat,
  categorization_unavailable: Bool,
  categorization_reason: String
) -> String {
  serialize_json(v: floor_component_receipt_json_value(
    workflow_name: workflow_name,
    run_id: run_id,
    head_sha: head_sha,
    rows: rows,
    selection_present: true,
    selection_mode_tag: selection_mode_tag,
    selected: selected,
    total: total,
    categorization_unavailable: categorization_unavailable,
    categorization_reason: categorization_reason,
    run_terminal_present: true,
    run_terminal_disposition: "incomplete" as NonEmptyStr,
    run_terminal_cause: run_terminal_cause,
    concluded_count: concluded_count,
    pending_from_index: pending_from_index
  ))
}

fn floor_component_receipt_document_with_selection(
  workflow_name: NonEmptyStr,
  run_id: NonEmptyStr,
  head_sha: CommitSha,
  rows: List<FloorComponentRow>,
  selection_mode_tag: NonEmptyStr,
  selected: Nat,
  total: Nat,
  categorization_unavailable: Bool,
  categorization_reason: String
) -> String {
  serialize_json(v: floor_component_receipt_json_value(
    workflow_name: workflow_name,
    run_id: run_id,
    head_sha: head_sha,
    rows: rows,
    selection_present: true,
    selection_mode_tag: selection_mode_tag,
    selected: selected,
    total: total,
    categorization_unavailable: categorization_unavailable,
    categorization_reason: categorization_reason,
    run_terminal_present: false,
    run_terminal_disposition: "concluded" as NonEmptyStr,
    run_terminal_cause: "none" as NonEmptyStr,
    concluded_count: count(rows),
    pending_from_index: 0
  ))
}
